  "upstream": {
    "note": "Source selection, revisions, stratum labels, and allocation counts replicate the Kimi K3 distribution-fidelity reference so methodology is comparable. Token IDs are not portable across tokenizers, so the suite itself must be minted per tokenizer family.",
    "artifact": "festr2/kimi-k3-distribution-fidelity-1024x2048-v1",
    "reference": "https://github.com/local-inference-lab/rtx6kpro/blob/master/models/kimi-k3/distribution-fidelity-1024x2048.md",
    "deviations": [
      "codeparrot/github-code is read from its parquet shards rather than through its loader script, which datasets 3 refuses to execute. The bytes and the pinned revision are unchanged.",
      "The structured-data stratum draws from the JSON, YAML, SQL, and protocol-buffer subsets of bigcode/starcoderdata rather than from codeparrot/github-code. github-code carries no structured-data files: its language table maps only to source-code extensions. common-pile/stackv2_edu_filtered, the other code source, turned out to be a documentation corpus - over 97 percent of its records are Markdown - so neither existing source could fill this stratum.",
      "GPQA-Diamond is pinned to Idavidrein/gpqa revision 633f5ee89ab8ad4522a9f850766b73f62147ffdd. The revision named in the reference belongs to an unnamed mirror and does not exist in the canonical repository."
    ]
  },
